# This repository *is* the contents of the CIRCUITPY drive, so it lives on a
# removable FAT volume that macOS, Windows and Linux all scribble on.  None
# of that belongs in git: tracking it means every `git pull` tries to write
# or delete files the operating system owns, and "System Volume Information"
# in particular is locked down on Windows, so a pull that tries stops there
# half-finished.
#
# Patterns are matched case-sensitively on a case-sensitive filesystem, so
# where an operating system picks an odd capitalisation it is spelled here
# exactly as that system writes it.

# --- written by the board itself ---
# saved admin settings
config.json
# CircuitPython version banner, rewritten on every boot
boot_out.txt
# may hold wifi credentials
settings.toml
# mount point for an SD card, if one is fitted
sd/

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.AppleDB
.AppleDesktop
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.documentrevisions-v100
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
.metadata_never_index
.metadata_never_index_unless_rootfs
.apdisk
# the custom-folder-icon file is literally "Icon" followed by a carriage return
Icon?

# --- Windows ---
System Volume Information
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.stackdump

# --- Linux ---
.Trash-*
.directory
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# --- local development ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
